# Copy to .env and fill in what you have. Everything is optional except at
# least one provider key.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   docker compose up -d

# --- Provider keys -----------------------------------------------------------
# A key on its own registers that provider. Delete the ones you do not use.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Also recognised without any further configuration:
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=
# TOGETHER_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# CEREBRAS_API_KEY=

# --- Your own key ------------------------------------------------------------
# The key YOUR apps send to mini-router. You invent this one -- it is not a
# provider key. mini-router checks it, then swaps in the provider's own key on
# the way out, so a client never sees a provider credential.
#
# Generate one:  openssl rand -hex 32
# Comma-separated for several, so you can revoke one device without the rest.
MINI_ROUTER_API_KEYS=

# --- Pools -------------------------------------------------------------------
# One client-facing name over several provider models, tried in the order
# written. Uncomment the line that matches the keys you actually filled in
# above: a pool naming a provider you have no key for stops mini-router from
# starting. Leave them blank and everything still works -- you just ask for
# real model names instead of a pool name.
#
# Both OpenAI and Anthropic:
#MINI_ROUTER_POOL_FAST=openai:gpt-4o-mini,anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5
#MINI_ROUTER_POOL_SMART=anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-5,openai:gpt-4o
#
# OpenAI only:
#MINI_ROUTER_POOL_FAST=openai:gpt-4o-mini
#MINI_ROUTER_POOL_SMART=openai:gpt-4o
MINI_ROUTER_POOL_FAST=
MINI_ROUTER_POOL_SMART=

# Apps with a hard-coded model name can reach a pool through an alias. Only
# set this once the pool it points at exists.
#MINI_ROUTER_ALIASES=gpt-3.5-turbo=fast,gpt-4o-mini=fast
MINI_ROUTER_ALIASES=

# --- A custom provider (a proxy or gateway) ----------------------------------
# For anything not in the list above: your own LiteLLM/vLLM box, a corporate
# gateway, an Azure deployment. Fill in all three or leave all three blank --
# a half-filled provider fails at startup with "needs a URL".
#
# The name MYPROXY is just an example; whatever you use here must match the
# MINI_ROUTER_PROVIDER_<NAME>_* variables in the compose file, and it is the
# name you reference in a pool (myproxy:some-model).
# Leave all three blank to have no custom provider at all. When you fill in
# the URL, set the protocol too: openai (most gateways) or anthropic.
MYPROXY_URL=
MYPROXY_PROTOCOL=
MYPROXY_API_KEY=
